#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below) \; 1: signal \, external FM modulator (fms 2 \, see FM), f 64;
#X obj 60 686 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 710 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 786 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 810 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. cut 60 (see the settings blocks below) \; delay flanger / chorus1 / chorus2 / slap / long / off \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices \, times bnd semitones \; n <name> <0-127>: a setting from a pot \, CV or MIDI CC \, \;   scaled to its range (switches in zones \, 64 = 0 if bipolar) \; nget <name> <tag>: outlet 3 gets norm <tag> <0-127> \, \;   the setting as a pot position (for pickup) \; disp <name>: outlet 3 gets disp <label> <value> \, \;   two symbols for a display (OLED) \; oled <host> <port>: changed settings to O2O (an OLED) as \;   OSC \, sent from a thread of its own \; oledtext <line 1> <line 2>: two lines for the OLED \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly, f 64;
#X obj 60 1206 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI\ CC\ (p8cc) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1230 [p8cc] at the top turns MIDI CC and 14-bit NRPN into n <name> <value> (any channel). \; Made for 4 rows of 16 controller pots: 8 groups of 8 \, CC 20-83 \, no setting twice: \; 20-27 PLAY: har1 har2 env1 env2 intv detn lev1 lev2 \; 28-35 FILTER: cut res egi env3 kbd vcut drv nois \; 36-43 OSC: oct1 oct2 pw1 pw2 pwm1 pwm2 hmg drft \; 44-51 WALSH-RING: wsh1 wsh2 wmx1 wmx2 wsm wse ring rmf \; 52-59 SYNC-FM: sync swp2 swe swm fm1 fm2 fmr fmhz \; 60-67 MG-FMSOURCE-DEG3: mgr mgi mgd mgv fms fmig pol trg \; 68-75 DELAY-EQ: dtim dfb dmf dmi dlev dgld treb bass \; 76-83 PERFORM: port pmod mono retr vamp bnd sprd mrph \; Without a pot: 84 env4 \, 85 trg4 \, 86 d4t1 \, 87 d4a1 \, 88 d4t2 \, 89 d4a2 \, 90 drvp \, 91 tone \, 92 leak \, 93 mgf \, 102 l2r \, 103 l2w \, 104 l2k \, 105 l2f \, 106 l2t1 \, 107 l2a1 \, 108 l2t2 \, 109 l2a2 \, 110 l3r \, 111 l3w \, 112 l3k \, 113 l3f \, 114 l3t1 \, 115 l3a1 \, 116 l3t2 \, 117 l3a2. \; NRPN: CC 99 = 0 \, CC 98 = the setting's CC number \, CC 6 = MSB \, CC 38 = LSB (only right after a CC 6 \, else CC 38 = pw1). \; Every continuous setting is smoothed over mrph ms (25) \, so CC steps become ramps., f 64;
#X obj 60 1594 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1618 0 har1 (45): Timbre of DCO1 \, one knob through all 15 distinct original timbres \, dark to bright: 0 16' / 9-64 saw net (16'2' \, 16'4'2' \, 16'4' \, 16'8'4' \, all at 45 \, 16'8'2' \, 16'8') / 73-127 square net (16'8' \, 16'8'4' \, 16'4' \, 16'4'2' \, all \, 16'8'2' \, 16'2'). One foot or the net per step \, no jumps. Combinations without 16' = oct1 2-4. \; 1 har2 (45): Timbre of DCO2 \, same path. \; 2 env1 (0): Envelope of DCO1 (DEG1) \, one knob: 0 gate / 1 very short pluck (no fade from the gate) / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. -1 = own values a1 ... r1. \; 3 env2 (0): Envelope of DCO2 (DEG2) \, the same \, -1 = own values a2 ... r2. \; 4 intv (0): Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 in semitones \, 0-12 \, as stored on the Poly-800 II. \; 5 detn (0): Detune of DCO2 downwards: the original's 4 steps 0 \, 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127. \; 6 lev1 (127): Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0): Level of DCO2 (every voice has both DCOs). Above full scale (lev1 + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 1966 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Timbre\ (har1\ /\ har2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1990 The 15 distinct timbres of the original \, dark to bright: \; 0: 16' / saw net 9: 16'2' / 18: 16'4'2' / 27: 16'4' / \; 36: 16'8'4' / 45: all / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: 16'8' / \; square net 73: 16'8' / 82: 16'8'4' / 91: 16'4' / \; 100: 16'4'2' / 109: all / 118: 16'8'2' / 127: 16'2'. \; One foot or the net per step. The combinations without 16' \; are the same waves higher: use oct1 / oct2 2-4. \; A fading foot rises in power \, so the morph has no dips., f 64;
#X obj 60 2146 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2170 Two read-only lists send presets to the object \, changing \; slots never writes anything back. Both send 'dump pdoly8 ...' \; messages (here via [s] \, nothing is wired across the patch). \; [p8factory]: the 64 Poly-800 II factory programs \, slot 0-63 \; (0 = program 11 \, 7 = 18 \, 8 = 21 ... 63 = 88) \, read from \; presets/poly800mk2-factory.txt next to the abstraction. \; [p8user name]: your own sounds in a [text define -k name] \; (saved with the patch). A slot number recalls\; only \; 'store N' writes: it stores the current sound in slot N \; (it needs outlet 2 of pdoly8~ at its right inlet \, here \; via [s]/[r]). 'write file' / 'read file' on the text \; define save and load banks. tools/p8sysex.py converts \; Poly-800 II sysex dumps to preset text and back., f 64;
#X floatatom 82 2388 4 0 63 0 factory - -;
