#X text 82 7688 l3t1 \, l3a1 \, l3t2 \, l3a2: the same for LFO3. \; 30 l3d: LFO3 depth x 0..2 \; 31 dtim: delay time x/: 2 \; 32 dlev: delay level +-15 \; har \, wsh \, wmx \, lev \, detn and drv follow per audio block (smoothed by mrph) \, all others per sample., f 64;
#X obj 60 7798 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Delay\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 7826 The digital delay of the Poly-800 II (71-75) \, measured: the echo is in phase on the left output and inverted on the right (a mono sum cancels it). A gate ends the echo train \, changing a value mutes the echo for a moment \, as on the original., f 64;
#X obj 460 7918 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 7894 6 0 99 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 7918 dtim \$1;
#X floatatom 160 7894 6 0 15 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 7918 dfb \$1;
#X text 82 7948 dtim (30): 0-99 = 4.2 ms - 1.08 s (70: 216 ms). \; dfb (0): feedback 0-15 (15: -3.1 dB per echo)., f 64;
#X obj 460 8008 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 7984 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 8008 dmf \$1;
#X floatatom 160 7984 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 8008 dmi \$1;
#X text 82 8038 dmf (0): mod rate 0-31 = 0.05-5 Hz. \; dmi (0): mod depth 0-31 (31: the time swings 1:5 \, about 10 dB less per 10 steps below)., f 64;
#X obj 460 8114 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 8090 6 0 15 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 8114 dlev \$1;
#X floatatom 160 8090 6 0 1 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 8114 dgld \$1;
#X obj 460 8144 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 60 8144 delay flanger;
#X msg 190 8144 delay chorus1;
#X msg 320 8144 delay chorus2;
#X msg 60 8178 delay slap;
#X msg 190 8178 delay long;
#X msg 320 8178 delay off;
#X text 82 8212 dlev (0): echo level 0-15 \, 0 = off. \; dgld (1): 1: changes glide (time like a tape \, feedback and level smoothed) \, for MIDI CC and modulation \, 0: every change mutes the echo for 40 ms \, as on the original. \; Presets: flanger (4 ms \, slow sweep \, feedback) \, chorus1 (fast \, shallow) \, chorus2 (slow \, wider) \, slap (120 ms) \, long (0.5 s with repeats) \, off., f 64;
#X obj 60 8338 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG1\ &\ DEG2\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 8366 Each voice's DCO1 and DCO2 have their own 6-stage DEG as on the Poly-800. Measured on a Poly-800 II: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, attack rises linearly (31: about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and release fall at a constant dB per second (31: about 18 s to -40 dB). env1 / env2 (Controls) morph through: 0 gate / 1 short pluck / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad., f 64;
#X obj 460 8506 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 8482 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 8506 a1 \$1;
#X floatatom 160 8482 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 8506 d1 \$1;
#X floatatom 260 8482 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 260 8506 bp1 \$1;
#X floatatom 360 8482 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 360 8506 sl1 \$1;
#X obj 460 8560 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 8536 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 8560 su1 \$1;
#X floatatom 160 8536 6 0 31 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 8560 r1 \$1;
#X text 82 8590 a1 d1 bp1 sl1 su1 r1: attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release of DEG1 (DCO1) \, 0-31. Setting one makes env1 -1., f 64;
